# The protocol form's server settings (/onboarding, /api/onboarding). Names only: never commit
# values. Set them for Production on Vercel; preview builds of branches don't get them, so a
# preview runs the form as an in-browser demo with no saving.

# The intake database (D85). Locally an embedded Postgres folder; in production the same
# h1-intake Neon project H1 AI Consulting uses (pooled string), so existing spas keep their
# answers and approvals. Migrations and the CLI use the unpooled one:
#   INTAKE_DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=... pnpm intake migrate
# Leave unset to run the form as an in-browser demo with no saving.
INTAKE_DATABASE_URL=pglite:.data/intake
# INTAKE_DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# AI name ideas, the role-play guest and the screenshot reader: Claude Haiku on Bedrock in H1's
# AWS account. The sign-off email: Amazon SES, from onboarding@h1aiconsulting.com. Locally the
# AWS CLI's `aws login` is enough. In production, an IAM user allowed only bedrock:InvokeModel on
# the Claude inference profiles and ses:SendEmail.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# INTAKE_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# INTAKE_AI_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5
# INTAKE_AI=off   turns the AI helpers off; the page uses its fixed lists and scripts

# Where the CLI's private links point (pnpm intake create-spa / new-link).
# SITE_URL=https://www.h1aiadvertising.com
